derivations.claim:
For a Verma-filtered $X$ induce on the flag length. For $X=0$ both sides vanish. For the top step $0	o K	o X	o\Delta(
u)	o0$ of a flag, exactness of $E\otimes-$ by [F4] gives an exact sequence $0	o E\otimes K	o E\otimes X	o E\otimes\Delta(
u)	o0$; by step 2.1 and the induction hypothesis $E\otimes K$ has a finite Verma flag with multiplicities $(E\otimes K:\Delta(\mu))=\sum_\eta\dim E_\eta(K:\Delta(\mu-\eta))$, and adjoining the flag of $E\otimes\Delta(
u)$ with multiplicities $\dim E_\eta\delta_{
u,\mu-\eta}$ gives a finite Verma flag of $E\otimes X$. Since multiplicity is additive along the resulting top step and $(X:\Delta(\mu-\eta))=(K:\Delta(\mu-\eta))+\delta_{
u,\mu-\eta}$ by [F1], the formula $(E\otimes X:\Delta(\mu))=\sum_\eta\dim E_\eta(X:\Delta(\mu-\eta))$ follows.
